# Unsure about "disgraceful". In S34 it is what "you and the world" agree on, which suggests conventional shame. In P1 it is disgrace as measured by pain or evil (S11). Polus accepts that measure, so I read both as one sense.
# "Pain" in the standard (S1, S11) may be pain to spectators, while in S22 it is pain to the injurer. But the argument's claim uses the injurer's pain throughout, so the claim keeps one sense.
